        <briefdescription>
<para>Computes divergent join points and cycle exits caused by branch divergence in <computeroutput>Term</computeroutput>. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This returns a pair of sets:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>The set of blocks which are reachable by disjoint paths from <computeroutput>Term</computeroutput>.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>The set also contains cycle exits if there two disjoint paths: one from <computeroutput>Term</computeroutput> to the cycle exit and another from <computeroutput>Term</computeroutput> to the cycle header. </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
